1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,200
The cavity tutorial, freshly copied: no Allrun and no logs. It has a decomposeParDict, but that alone does not mean it runs in parallel.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:12,800
So FoDE suggests blockMesh and icoFoam, run serially.

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:18,800
Tick Also create Allrun-parallel: decomposePar and reconstructPar are added around the solver, marked for the parallel script only.

4
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:23,830
The steps before the solver go in Allrun.pre, which both scripts call.

5
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:28,362
Allrun calls it, then runs icoFoam serially.

6
00:00:28,362 --> 00:00:37,198
Allrun-parallel calls it too, then decomposes the case, runs icoFoam on nine processors and puts the results back together.

7
00:00:37,198 --> 00:00:41,798
A step the logs cannot show goes in with Add Command.

8
00:00:41,798 --> 00:00:46,799
An OpenFOAM application is written with runApplication, so it writes a log like every other step.

9
00:00:46,799 --> 00:00:56,867
Create writes all four scripts and opens the Allrun.

10
00:00:56,867 --> 00:01:05,400
With both scripts, Allrun Steps asks which one to follow.

11
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:12,647
Run Allrun Script asks too.

12
00:01:12,647 --> 00:01:16,647
Allrun-parallel runs: blockMesh from Allrun.pre, decomposePar, icoFoam on nine processors, reconstructPar, then postProcess.
